  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan drops Divine Thief Lu Zuan Feng into a roadside clash with Tie Ruo Nan’s group, the seven Tie clansmen turn pale because the clan had kept the news confidential. Narration says even Wu clan and Shang clan had no knowledge of that humiliation. Tie Ba Xiu tries to dismiss the claim as nonsense, while Tie Ruo Nan reads it as blackmail to trade for Bai Ning Bing’s life and demands how an outsider at the mountain learned the secret. Fang Yuan laughs that he spoke casually and names the move as besieging the stronghold to strike the reinforcements.",
      "chapters": [
        359
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_tie_ruo_nan",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "fac_shang_clan",
        "char_tie_ba_xiu",
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later judges that Divine Thief Lu Zuan Feng should already have repeatedly infiltrated Demon Suppression Tower and caused great havoc, so Tie clan cannot gather strength against him for a month or two.",
      "chapters": [
        365
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "divine-thief-reputation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_demon_suppression_tower",
        "fac_tie_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later Southern Border summary again calls him a rank five Gu Master known as the Divine Thief, notes a demonic path Gu Immortal backing him and his prior sneak into Tie clan’s Demon Suppression Tower, and states he used infiltration methods to kill Wu Shen Tong and end Yi Tian Village’s first righteous path crisis.",
      "chapters": [
        965
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "divine-thief-reputation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "sys_gu_master",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_wu_shen_tong",
        "loc_yi_tian_village"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the village ranking after Chou Jiu’s rise, Lu Zuan Feng holds second place behind Xiao Shan.",
      "chapters": [
        966
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "divine-thief-reputation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chou_jiu",
        "char_xiao_shan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mountain news then says Lu Zuan Feng’s repeated secret infiltrations disturbed Tie Mu Bai’s closed cultivation. Tie Mu Bai personally struck; though Lu Zuan Feng was a famous divine thief and rank five Gu Master, he took serious injuries and barely escaped. After Tie clan settled that matter, its gaze turned to San Cha Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        370
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tie-mu-bai-strike",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_mu_bai",
        "loc_san_cha_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He carefully and softly urges his master that Xiao clan’s ancestor, a rank seven Gu Immortal, has requested a meeting and has already waited outside for two hours.",
      "chapters": [
        999
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yi-tian-mountain-mission",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_xiao_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His master, rank seven lone cultivator Old Man Yue Xia, sends him to Yi Tian Mountain to solve Xiao Shan’s crisis and blows cold air into his belly as Immortal Gu support. That evening rank five Gu Master Lu Zuan Feng infiltrates the righteous path camp, assassinates Wu Shen Tong, and brings back the head. He then speaks modestly so the camp cannot easily ruin his fame by overpraise.",
      "chapters": [
        1000
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yi-tian-mountain-mission",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_yi_tian_mountain",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later narration, weighing why lone immortals would not attack without reservation, names Old Man Yue Xia’s treasured disciple Lu Zuan Feng as present on Yi Tian Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        1001
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yi-tian-mountain-mission",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He later charges in with Xiao Shan and another rank five Gu Master and their troops.",
      "chapters": [
        1002
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yi-tian-mountain-mission",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
